IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rta-types`

-- Residential Tenancies Act 1986 — GOAL 4: ENTRY AND BOARDING HOUSES.
--
--   "May the landlord enter on this notice; is this boarding house
--    termination lawful; and when does a boarding house tenancy end?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1986_120.txt — ss 48,
-- 66D, 66R-66X.

§ `Goal 4 — entry and boarding houses`

-- Hours between two moments, each a date and an hour of the day (0-24, as a
-- decimal: 17.5 is 5.30 pm).
GIVEN d1 IS A DATE, h1 IS A NUMBER, d2 IS A DATE, h2 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the hours from` d1 `at` h1 `to` d2 `at` h2 MEANS
    (Day d2 MINUS Day d1) TIMES 24 PLUS (h2 MINUS h1)

§§ `Entry to premises (s 48)`

-- s 48(2) "The landlord may enter the premises— (a) in any case of emergency;
-- or (b) for the purpose of inspecting the premises, at any time between 8
-- o'clock in the morning and 7 o'clock in the evening on a day specified in a
-- notice given to the tenant not less than 48 hours nor more than 14 days
-- before the intended entry, and not more frequently than once in any period
-- of 4 weeks; or (ba) for the purpose of testing for ... contaminants ...
-- between 8 ... and 7 ..., after giving ... notice ... at least 48 hours but
-- not more than 14 days before ...; or (c) [to check remedial work] ...
-- between 8 ... and 7 ... specified in a notice given ... not less than 48
-- hours nor more than 14 days before ...; or (ca) [smoke alarms] ... (cb)
-- [healthy homes] ... (cc) [decontamination] ... (d) [necessary repairs or
-- maintenance] ... between 8 ... and 7 ..., after giving ... notice ... at
-- least 24 hours before the intended entry". s 48 "(2A) Subsection (2B)
-- applies if— (a) there is rent that is at least 14 days in arrear; and (b)
-- the landlord has reasonable cause to believe that the tenant has abandoned
-- the premises. (2B) The landlord may enter ... to confirm ... at any time
-- specified in a notice given to the tenant not less than 24 hours before".
-- "Once in any period of 4 weeks": at least 28 days after the last inspection
-- entry (fork F6). Entry on consent or by order of the Tribunal is not this
-- function's question.
@ref s 48(1)-(2B)
@export Whether a landlord may enter the premises on notice under s 48 of the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ): in an emergency at any time; for an inspection between 8 am and 7 pm on 48 hours' to 14 days' notice and no more than once in 4 weeks; for contaminant testing or checking remedial work between 8 am and 7 pm on 48 hours' to 14 days' notice; for smoke alarms, healthy homes, decontamination or necessary repairs between 8 am and 7 pm on 24 hours' notice; and to confirm abandonment, with rent 14 days in arrear and reasonable cause, on 24 hours' notice. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN e IS AN `Entry notice`  @desc The purpose, when notice was given and when entry is to be made (dates and hours), the last inspection entry, the days of rent in arrear, and whether the landlord has reasonable cause to believe the premises abandoned
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the landlord may enter` e IF
    CONSIDER e's `purpose`
    WHEN `(2)(a) emergency` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `(2)(b) inspection` THEN
            daytime AND notice AT LEAST 48 AND notice AT MOST 14 TIMES 24
        AND (CONSIDER e's `last inspection entry on`
             WHEN JUST last THEN Day (e's `entry on`) MINUS Day last AT LEAST 28
             WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE)
    WHEN `(2)(ba) contaminant testing` THEN daytime AND notice AT LEAST 48 AND notice AT MOST 14 TIMES 24
    WHEN `(2)(c) checking remedial work` THEN daytime AND notice AT LEAST 48 AND notice AT MOST 14 TIMES 24
    WHEN `(2)(ca)-(cc), (d) smoke alarms, healthy homes, decontamination or necessary repairs` THEN daytime AND notice AT LEAST 24
    WHEN `(2A)-(2B) confirming abandonment` THEN
            e's `days of rent in arrear` AT LEAST 14
        AND e's `reasonable cause to believe the premises abandoned`
        AND notice AT LEAST 24
    WHERE
        daytime MEANS e's `entry at hour` AT LEAST 8 AND e's `entry at hour` AT MOST 19
        notice MEANS `the hours from` (e's `entry notice given on`) `at` (e's `entry notice given at hour`) `to` (e's `entry on`) `at` (e's `entry at hour`)

§§ `Boarding houses (ss 66D, 66R-66X)`

-- s 66D "(1) If 1 week's rent or less is received as bond under a boarding
-- house tenancy,— (a) the bond need not be lodged ...; and (b) the landlord
-- must immediately give the tenant a receipt ...; and (c) the landlord must
-- refund the bond to the tenant when the tenancy terminates."
@ref s 66D(1)
GIVEN weeks IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a boarding house bond need not be lodged, weeks of rent` weeks IF
    weeks AT MOST 1

-- s 66R "(2) The landlord may also enter the room of a tenant if the
-- landlord— (a) gives the tenant ..., at least 24 hours before the entry, a
-- notice of entry that complies with section 66S; and (b) enters the room
-- only for the purpose set out in the notice ...; and (c) enters the room
-- between 8 am and 6 pm."
@ref ss 66R(2), 66S
GIVEN r IS A `Boarding room entry`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the landlord may enter the boarding room on notice` r IF
        r's `notice for a s 66S(1) purpose, with the s 66S(3) content`
    AND `the hours from` (r's `room entry notice given on`) `at` (r's `room entry notice given at hour`) `to` (r's `room entered on`) `at` (r's `room entered at hour`) AT LEAST 24
    AND r's `room entered at hour` AT LEAST 8
    AND r's `room entered at hour` AT MOST 18

-- s 66U "(1) The landlord of a boarding house may terminate a boarding house
-- tenancy— (a) immediately, if the tenant has— (i) caused, or threatened to
-- cause, serious damage ...; or (ii) endangered ... people or property; or
-- (iii) caused ... serious disruption to other tenants; or (b) on 48 hours'
-- notice, if— (i) the landlord has, by written notice ..., required the
-- tenant to pay any rent in arrears within a stated period of not less than
-- 10 days ..., and the tenant fails to pay ...; or (ii) the tenant is using
-- the premises for an illegal purpose; or (iii) the landlord believes, having
-- complied with section 66X, that the tenant has abandoned the room; or (c) on
-- 14 days' notice, if the tenancy is also a service tenancy ...; or (d) on 28
-- days' notice, if no reason is given." s 66V "(1) A tenant ... may terminate
-- the tenancy by giving at least 48 hours' notice ... (2) A tenant need not
-- give notice in writing."
@ref ss 66U(1)-(2), 66V
GIVEN g IS A `Boarding house ground`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum hours of notice for a boarding house termination on` g MEANS
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `s 66U(1)(a) serious damage, endangering people or property, or serious disruption` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 66U(1)(c) also a service tenancy` THEN 14 TIMES 24
    WHEN `s 66U(1)(d) no reason given` THEN 28 TIMES 24
    OTHERWISE 48

@ref ss 66U, 66V
@export Whether a notice terminating a boarding house tenancy is lawful under ss 66U and 66V of the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ): immediately for serious damage, endangerment or serious disruption; on 48 hours' notice for unpaid arrears after a written notice of at least 10 days, illegal use, or abandonment; on 14 days' notice for a service tenancy; on 28 days' notice with no reason; and by the tenant on 48 hours' notice; a landlord's notice in writing with the s 66U(2) content. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN n IS A `Boarding house notice`  @desc The ground, when the notice was given and when termination takes effect (dates and hours), whether the notice is in the required form, and for arrears the period the arrears notice allowed and whether the arrears were paid
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the boarding house termination is lawful` n IF
        n's `boarding notice in the required form`
    AND `the hours from` (n's `boarding notice given on`) `at` (n's `boarding notice given at hour`) `to` (n's `termination takes effect on`) `at` (n's `termination takes effect at hour`)
            AT LEAST `the minimum hours of notice for a boarding house termination on` (n's `boarding house ground`)
    AND (    NOT n's `boarding house ground` EQUALS `s 66U(1)(b)(i) rent arrears unpaid after a notice of at least 10 days`
         OR (    n's `arrears notice period stated, in days` AT LEAST 10
             AND NOT n's `arrears paid within the stated period`))

-- s 66W "A boarding house tenancy terminates 48 hours after the death of a
-- sole tenant". s 66X "(2) The landlord must not enter the room until at
-- least 24 hours after putting the notice on the door. ... (4) The notice of
-- termination must specify the date and time on which the tenancy
-- terminates, which must be a time no sooner than 48 hours after the notice
-- is put on the door."
@ref ss 66W, 66X(2), (4)
GIVEN hrs IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE, h IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar day` hrs `hours after` d `at hour` h MEANS
    Date (Day d PLUS FLOOR ((h PLUS hrs) DIVIDED BY 24))
